1) GIA Header Generation:
-------------------------

Set up:
Download the interrupt database and pass it to gen-gia-intr-header.py

Usage:
$ python3 <base_path>/gen-gia-intr-header.py <root_dir_of_interrupt_tracker_data> > irq-gia-google-lga.txt

-------------------------
2) GIA Device Tree Generation
-------------------------

Setup:
* Download the interrupt tracker database (TODO: Add instructions to readme. b/359937751)
* Download the base address map for the chipset you want as CSV. For MBU, this is go/mbu-soc-memory-map

Usage:
$ python gen-gia-device-tree.py -i <root_of_interrupt_tracker_data> -b <sswrp_base_addr_map_csv> [OPTIONAL: -s <soc> | -a <manual_address_csv> | -d | -p <power_domains_csv>]

Arguments:
--addresses, -a:	Provide a CSV with format <gia_name>, <address offset>.
			This is used to manually specify the address for GIA nodes which are missing from interrupt tracker data.
			Any GIAs where address cannot be found will be output with an address ending in 'ffff' and the node disabled
--base_addr_map, -b:	Provide a base addr map CSV like go/mbu-soc-memory-map.
-d:			Turns on debug logging
--hack-pds, -H:		Sets power domains to sswrp_<sswrp>_pd, if one exists in the power-controller DT node for the SSWRP. When combined with -p, the power domain CSV takes precedence
--intr_tracker, -i:	Provide the base directory of the interrupt tracker.
			This path will be searched recursively for files named *_launch_o.csv and *_gia_map.csv to generate the device tree. Small note on perfomance: the amount of path traversal in this directory is the single largest factor in script execution time.
--power_domains, -p:	Provide a CSV with format <gia_name>, <power_domain>
			This is used to generate a device tree with power domains
			Not providing this will generate nodes with no power domains
--soc, -s:		Provide the 3 letter SOC name.
			If not provided, defaults to MBU

-------------------------
3) GIC Header Generation
-------------------------

Setup:
* Download the Interrupt CSV for the chipset & label you want

Usage:
$ python gen-gic-intr-header.py <interrupts.csv> -s <SOC> [OPTIONAL -d | -c <YEAR>] > <soc_gic.h>

Arguments:
'-c', '--copyright_year': 	Provide the copyright year to use. If not provided, defaults to today's year
-d:				Turns on debug logging
--soc, -s:			Provide the 3 letter SOC name. If not provided, defaults to MBU
